{"name":"Shadow Dance","hex":"#877d83","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"shadow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dark image projected onto a surface where light (or other radiation) is blocked by the shade of an object.","Relative darkness, especially as caused by the interruption of light; gloom; obscurity."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Unofficial, informal, unauthorized, but acting as though it were.","Having power or influence, but not widely known or recognized."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shadow"},{"term":"dance","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sequence of rhythmic steps or movements usually performed to music, for pleasure or as a form of social interaction.","A social gathering where dancing is the main activity."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To move with rhythmic steps or movements, especially in time to music.","To leap or move lightly and rapidly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dance"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shadow Dance (novel)","blocks":[{"text":"Shadow Dance was Angela Carter's first novel, published in England by Heinemann in 1966. It was published under the name Honeybuzzard in the United States. Upon publication it was acclaimed by Anthony Burgess, who wrote that he \"read this book with admiration, horror and other relevant emotions... Angela Carter has remarkable descriptive gifts, a powerful imagination, and... a capacity for looking at the mess of contemporary life without flinching.\""}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d2/Shadow_Dance_%28Angela_Carter_novel_-_cover_art%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shadow_Dance_(novel)"},{"title":"Shadow","blocks":[{"text":"A shadow is a dark area on a surface where light from a light source is blocked by an object. In contrast, shade occupies the three-dimensional volume behind an object with light in front of it. The cross-section of a shadow is a two-dimensional silhouette, or a reverse projection of the object blocking the light."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/The_shadow_of_a_musician_playing_transverse_flute.jpg/330px-The_shadow_of_a_musician_playing_transverse_flute.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shadow"},{"title":"Dance","blocks":[{"text":"Dance is an art form, consisting of sequences of body movements with aesthetic and often symbolic value, either improvised or purposefully selected. Dance can be categorized and described by its choreography, by its repertoire of movements or by its historical period or place of origin. Dance is typically performed with musical accompaniment, and sometimes with the dancer simultaneously using a musical instrument themselves."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Two_dancers.jpg/330px-Two_dancers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dance"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d2/Shadow_Dance_%28Angela_Carter_novel_-_cover_art%29.jpg/250px-Shadow_Dance_%28Angela_Carter_novel_-_cover_art%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d2/Shadow_Dance_%28Angela_Carter_novel_-_cover_art%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d2/Shadow_Dance_%28Angela_Carter_novel_-_cover_art%29.jpg/250px-Shadow_Dance_%28Angela_Carter_novel_-_cover_art%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"First edition","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AShadow_Dance_(Angela_Carter_novel_-_cover_art).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/